---
title: Images and icon atlases
description: Show declared images, reuse icons in virtualized lists, and display an atlas region.
---

<span hidden data-pagefind-filter="SDK:development image resources"></span>

This page describes the unreleased desktop image-resource work. Check your
host with `PlatformService:Supports("ImageRegion")` before using an atlas.

## Show one image

Add `"Logo.png"` to the `Assets` list in `lui.json` and place the PNG beside the
manifest. This fragment assumes an existing `Window`.

```luau
local Logo = Instance.new("ImageLabel", {
    Parent = Window,
    Source = "Logo.png",
    Size = UDim2.fromOffset(32, 32),
    AccessibilityLabel = "Application logo",
})
```

The host starts loading after the property assignment. Read `LoadState` or
subscribe to `LoadChanged` if the application needs to show a fallback.

## Show one tile from an atlas

Declare both `Toolbar.png` and `Save.png` in `Assets`. This example uses a
24×24 tile whose top-left pixel is at (48, 24) in `Toolbar.png`.

```luau
local Platform = app:GetService("PlatformService")
local SaveIcon = Instance.new("ImageLabel", {
    Parent = Window,
    Size = UDim2.fromOffset(20, 20),
    Source = "Save.png",
    AccessibilityLabel = "Save",
})

if Platform:Supports("ImageRegion") then
    SaveIcon.SourceRectOffset = Vector2.new(48, 24)
    SaveIcon.SourceRectSize = Vector2.new(24, 24)
    SaveIcon.Source = "Toolbar.png"
end
```

WinUI and GTK fit the selected region inside the control while preserving its
aspect ratio. Source coordinates use physical pixels and control geometry uses
logical units. Values must be whole numbers from 0 through 4096. Set
`SourceRectSize` to `Vector2.new(0, 0)` to display the full image again. An
out-of-bounds region is blank while the source retains its loading state.
Reserve a gutter of matching edge pixels around each atlas tile to reduce
color bleed at fractional display scales.

## Virtualized and thumbnail-heavy views

- Recycle visible row controls and update `Source` when a row's asset changes.
  Controls that reference the same name share the decoded source. Keep the
  number of outstanding loads under 32 by requesting visible rows first.
- An independent icon is a good default. An atlas can reduce first-use
  decodes and the number of asset declarations for a stable icon set. Changing
  the displayed tile does not request a new decode.
- Declare static thumbnails at their presentation sizes. Desktop decoding
  admits PNG and JPEG up to 1 MiB encoded, 4,096 pixels per side, and 1,048,576
  pixels total. Inactive large images retire when no control uses them. Clear
  `Source` or destroy the view when an image leaves the live UI.
- The private desktop profiles keep an application-wide 32 MiB decoded pixel
  budget. There is no app cache configuration. Use a supported FrameSurface
  for a continuously updated viewport. A FileService selection grants file
  access through that service and does not assign a new ImageLabel asset name.

## Show a generated thumbnail

```luau
local Assets = app:GetService("AssetService")
local Pixels = buffer.create(32 * 32 * 4)
-- An opaque gray BGRA pixel has alpha 255 and identical color channels.
for Offset = 0, buffer.len(Pixels) - 4, 4 do
    buffer.writeu32(Pixels, Offset, 0xff808080)
end
local Thumbnail, Failure = Assets:FromPixels(Pixels, 32, 32, 128, "BGRA8Premultiplied")
if Thumbnail then
    local Label = Instance.new("ImageLabel", {
        Parent = Window,
        Size = UDim2.fromOffset(32, 32),
        ImageResource = Thumbnail,
    })
    -- Bind other visible rows to Thumbnail while it is open.
    -- Close when the app has finished making new bindings to this resource.
    Thumbnail:Close()
end
```

Check `PlatformService:Supports("RuntimeImages")` for desktop presentation.
The handle owns a copy of your buffer. Existing labels keep their bindings
after the handle closes. Destroy a label or clear its `ImageResource` to drop
that binding. To reuse a thumbnail after scrolling off-screen, keep its
handle open while it remains in your model.

## Show a user-selected image

Use the `Files` module with the existing `Dialogs` grant. After
`Picker:OpenFile` supplies a `Document`, pass its authorized bytes to the
same asset service.

```luau
local Assets = app:GetService("AssetService")
Document:Read(function(Bytes, ReadFailure)
    Document:Close()
    if not Bytes then return end
    local Resource, DecodeFailure = Assets:FromEncoded(Bytes)
    if Resource then
        Preview.ImageResource = Resource
        Resource:Close()
    end
end)
```

Handle read and source-creation errors in the app's status UI. Use
`LoadChanged` and `LoadState` to handle full decode failures, even when
`FromEncoded` recognized valid dimensions. A virtualized view can cancel
the file operation and clear or replace its label while scrolling.

In a large workbench, keep only viewport rows and a short look-ahead pool
bound to image controls. Reuse immutable thumbnail handles for entries the
user may revisit, and close handles when their model entries retire. Use a
generation or row identity when applying a late result so a recycled row
keeps its current preview. Keep thumbnail generation and result delivery
bounded independently from the FrameSurface viewport.
